Exceptions – a “Delayed” Transaction Modification Request
When you make direct changes to fields in the transaction, they take effect immediately. 
In many cases, this works fine, but there are situations where you want to hold off on 
updating the transaction until all the changes are in place. A typical example of this is CRC 
fields. It makes little sense to calculate a CRC field if another transaction field on which the 
CRC depends will be changing.
