Creating a Factory Exception
In addition to the above callback exceptions, there is another type of exception: Instead of 
it being associated with user-specified callback code, it occurs automatically each time the 
callback function is called (even if there is no user-specified callback code). This allows 
you to generate randomized error injections.
Note that factory exceptions and callbacks are mutually exclusive: If a user modifies the 
transaction in the callback, the factory exception will not occur.
The code to set up a factory exception is similar to the code in Creating an Exception 
above, with a few minor differences.
